What was calculated
Using Quantum ESPRESSO (DFT-PBE) via qmatsuite, I ran the 4-step band-structure workflow on the diamond-structure silicon primitive cell (Fd-3m, 2 atoms, SSSP precision pseudopotentials):

SCF → NSCF → bands.x (k-path) → post-processing — all four steps completed successfully.

Results
Silicon band structure

The bands were computed along the high-symmetry path L → Γ → X → U → Γ (91 k-points, 8 bands). Energies are referenced to the valence-band maximum.

Quantity	Value
Indirect band gap	0.65 eV
VBM location	Γ
CBM location	along Γ→X (~85% toward X)
Direct gap at Γ	2.54 eV
Fermi energy	5.76 eV
Total energy	−310.75 eV
This reproduces the textbook picture of silicon: an indirect semiconductor with the valence maximum at Γ and the conduction minimum near X. The 0.65 eV gap is the expected PBE underestimate of the experimental ~1.17 eV value — a standard limitation of semilocal DFT functionals, not an error in the calculation.

